results.description:
This is a scene based on how it was back in the 80's, relaxing days as kids, playing the first NES and its amazing games at night, before dinner, alongside the people who love you in the living room, in a comfy sofa.
Unfortunately, I was not born in that year, but I tried to reimagine on how it was.

This was made in Autodesk Maya and Substance Painter.

This scene, or you could call it a collection, contains:
A plane that is supposed to be part of a room;
An armchair;
A commode/chest of drawers;
A CRT Panasonic TV;
A couple of windows;
Cables all around the room;
The Nintendo Entertainment System;
A couple of games/cartridges lying around;
A couple of boxes from those games lying around;
A couple of Nintendo's famous magazine, Nintendo Power;
The controllers;
The Zapper guns;
The boxes of the controllers and of the NES;
A plug;

Hopefully, a sense of nostalgia to all of you!
